CLEAN UP

  The unpainted surfaces are coated with a waxy oil to prevent corrosion during
  shipment. Remove this protective coating with a solvent cleaner or degreaser. For
  thorough cleaning, some parts must be removed.

  For optimum performance, clean all moving parts or sliding contact surfaces. Avoid
  chlorine-based solvents, such as acetone or brake parts cleaner that may damage
  painted surfaces.

  Always follow the manufacturer's instructions when using cleaning products.

            WARNING: PETROL AND PETROLEUM BASED PRODUCTS HAVE LOW
            FLASHPOINTS AND CAN EXPLODE OR CAUSE FIRE IF USED TO
            CLEAN MACHINERY. DO NOT USE THESE PRODUCTS TO CLEAN THE
            MACHINERY.

            CAUTION: MANY CLEANING SOLVENTS ARE TOXIC IF INHALED. MINIMIZE
            YOUR RISK BY ONLY USING THESE PRODUCTS IN A WELL VENTILATED
            AREA.

